# Infrastructure & DevOps Rules - Arcanovi Project

## Docker-First Architecture

**Container Strategy**: All components run in optimized Docker containers with proper networking and volume management.

**Service Orchestration**: Docker Compose for development, container orchestration for production.

**Environment Consistency**: Identical container behavior across development, staging, and production.

## Container Configuration

### Django Backend Container
- Multi-stage builds for optimized production images
- Non-root user execution for security
- Health check endpoints for container monitoring
- Gunicorn with async workers for SSE support (optional)
- Environment-based configuration management
- Proper signal handling for graceful shutdowns

### React Frontend Container
- Nginx-based serving for static assets
- Build-time environment variable injection
- Gzip compression and caching headers
- Security headers (CSP, HSTS, X-Frame-Options)
- SSL/TLS termination configuration
- Progressive Web App service worker setup

### Database Configuration
- PostgreSQL with proper initialization scripts
- Volume mounting for data persistence
- Backup and restore automation
- Connection pooling optimization
- Read replica setup for scaling
- Database health monitoring

### Session Management Configuration
- Database-based session storage (no Redis dependency)
- Django's built-in session framework
- Session cleanup management commands
- Memory optimization for session data
- Connection pooling for Django
- Session security and expiration policies

## Nginx Reverse Proxy

### SSE-Optimized Configuration (Optional)
```nginx
location /api/stream_ai_response {
    proxy_http_version 1.1;
    proxy_set_header Connection "";
    proxy_buffering off;
    proxy_cache off;
    proxy_read_timeout 3600s;
    proxy_pass http://django-backend:8000;
}
```

### Performance Optimization
- HTTP/2 support with proper multiplexing
- Gzip compression for text-based responses
- Static asset caching with appropriate headers
- Rate limiting for API endpoints
- SSL/TLS optimization with modern cipher suites
- Keep-alive connection management

### Security Configuration
- CORS header management for cross-origin requests
- Request size limits to prevent DoS attacks
- IP whitelisting for administrative endpoints
- Security headers injection
- DDoS protection and rate limiting
- Log analysis for security monitoring

